{'id': 'arc_opposite_edge_bar_marker_beams_segment_offset_mapping', 'kind': 'memory', 'title': 'ARC opposite-edge bar marker beams with segment-offset mapping', 'content': "For ARC grids with a uniform background, two equal-length solid bars on opposite borders, and sparse interior markers, use the bars as parallel beam anchors. A marker's coordinate along the bar span determines its corresponding coordinate on the opposite bar span by preserving the offset from the start of each span. On the marker side, replace each marker with color 4 and fill the straight segment from it to the nearby bar using the marker color, leaving the bar intact. At the corresponding offset on the opposite bar, extend a full perpendicular line from that border bar toward the far border, in the marker color; preserve the source bar. This works in either orientation: vertical side bars produce horizontal beams, and top/bottom bars produce vertical beams. Demonstrations: vertical bars and markers colored 9 produced 4 at each marker, 9 between markers and nearby bars, plus full 9 lines at mapped offsets across the opposite bar's region. A separate case with color 3 showed a single marker projecting a full line at the same relative row offset. Validate segment lengths, span ordering, and untouched bar cells.", 'path': 'arc', 'scope': 'global', 'reference': {}, 'arguments': {}, 'metadata': {}, 'source': 'agent', 'created_at': '2026-09-29T12:48:33.941630+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-09-29T12:48:33.941650+00:00', 'version': 1}

